  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support market system development on ground nuts production and value addition in Yirol East.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CTP has been providing seeds and tools to communities in Yirol East through its local partner CDoR for the past 7 years. The project was being funded by HPP (Irish Aid) that ended in December 2023, UKAM and Caritas Norway with both projects ending in December 2024. The project reached 800 HHs under HPP, 800HHs under Caritas and 3,200HHs under UKAM. The households were provided with agricultural inputs (seeds, tools, and ox-ploughs). According to the post-harvest assessment conducted by CTP and Local Partner, 55% of those supported reported that their harvest has increased compared to previous years and 66% of the farmers reported that they have reserved seeds for planting in the next season. The provision of seeds and ox-ploughs enabled farmers to increase the size of their farmlands. CTP noted through assessments and post-harvest surveys that groundnut production is one of the key cash crops which was most preferred by the communities because of its value addition elements. CTP anticipates that the growth in supporting market systems can increase productivity and enterprise wealth and inclusive growth in end markets that will subsequently reduce poverty. CTP and its partner CDoR will also use this as an opportunity to transition the assistance from a direct support approach to a market system-based approach as an exit strategy.</narrative>
  </description>
